AB  - This study analyzes the influence of Systemic Methodology, represented in the ID-Think® Product model, on the development of key competencies in the Bachelor's Degree in Industrial Design and Product Development Engineering at the Polytechnic University of Valencia. A quantitative approach with a descriptive and cross-sectional design was applied. The sample consisted of 18 students, and a structured ad hoc questionnaire, validated by expert judgment, was used. Perceptions of dimensions such as creativity, organization, problem solving, and collaborative work were evaluated. The results show that the model improves efficiency in design and decision-making, although its structure may limit creativity for some students. It is concluded that ID-Think® is a valuable tool in the educational context, but greater methodological flexibility is recommended to enhance its impact on innovation and autonomy. © 2026, Centro de Informacion Tecnologica. All rights reserved.
