AB  - This dataset contains questionnaire responses on preservice teachers’ self-reported scientific literacy-related competencies, applications, perceived importance, enhancement measures, and determinants in Vietnam. The dataset comprises 807 anonymized and complete responses collected in May 2025 through an online Vietnamese-language questionnaire administered via Google Forms. It includes 42 five-point Likert-scale items and six background variables covering gender, year of study, academic performance, teaching practicum experience, perceived necessity of scientific literacy, and readiness to apply scientific literacy. The questionnaire items are organized into five scientific literacy-related dimensions: global scientific literacy competence, application of scientific literacy competence, perceived importance of scientific literacy competence, suggested measures for enhancing scientific awareness, and determinants of scientific literacy competence. The data repository contains the respondent-level dataset, a codebook, the original Vietnamese questionnaire, an English translation, and a README file. These materials may be reused for descriptive analysis, subgroup comparison, reliability assessment, exploratory factor re-examination, scale refinement, instrument adaptation, and cross-context comparison in teacher education and science education research. Copyright © 2026. Published by Elsevier Inc.
