TI  - GuidePrompt-EDU: Leveraging Prompt Engineering to Integrate Generative AI into Pre-Service Teacher Education
PY  - 2026
Y1  - 2026
T2  - 2026 IEEE Global Engineering Education Conference (EDUCON)
SP  - 1
EP  - 9
DO  - 10.1109/educon67543.2026.11574140
AB  - The growing presence of AI in education demands teacher training to integrate GenAI, a issue given the scarcity of educators and high dropout rates in teacher programs, especially in Mathematics. This research aimed to investigate GenAI's potential in Basic Education, focusing on the initial training of Mathematics teachers through the development and validation of the GuidePrompt-EDU. The guide is a prompt engineering adaptation, aligning commands with BNCC competences to offer a practical and pedagogically clear resource. The methodology, qualitative-quantitative and exploratory, involved the tool's adaptation, an experimentation workshop, and pedagogical validation by specialists via a Likert questionnaire. Initial results indicated that, while participants recognized the clarity and utility of the GuidePrompt-EDU for planning Mathematics lessons, significant uncertainty was identified regarding its practical classroom application. The study concludes that the GuidePrompt-EDU is a promising proposal for critical GenAI integration into teacher training. It emphasizes the crucial need to deepen this formation, integrating theoretical discussions, pedagogical practices, and ethical aspects to ensure that future educators use technology in an autonomous and innovative way, aligned with contemporary demands. © 2026 IEEE.
