DO  - 10.1016/j.procs.2025.07.243
AB  - This article describes the MG-MOOC methodology for the design and implementation of Massive Open Online Course (MOOC) based on gamification and m-learning techniques, aimed at training 199 university professors from 22 public and private institutions in Antioquia, Colombia. The objective was to strengthen their competencies in essential functions: teaching, research, outreach-internationalization, and academic management, under pedagogical and technological quality standards. Using a mixed research approach (exploratory, descriptive, explanatory, and field-based), the sample of professors was selected probabilistically from institutions recognized by the Ministry of National Education (MEN). Data collection involved a validated questionnaire (Cronbach's alpha α=0.92), interviews, and documentary analysis. The process was developed in four phases: (1) identification of training needs in teaching, research, outreach, and academic management; (2) MOOC design; (3) MOOC development; and (4) validation and implementation using a technological platform called EDUPROFE. The results demonstrated that a structured methodology for the design, creation, and implementation of MOOCs improves the efficiency of the training process. In conclusion, the study shows that the application of the MG-MOOC methodology, based on gamification and mobile learning principles, not only strengthens teachers' competencies in various academic functions, but also offers a replicable and scalable model for continuing education initiatives in similar contexts. The integration of technological tools with a rigorous pedagogical approach contributes significantly to improving educational quality at the higher education level. © 2025 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V.
