TI  - Evaluating the Impact of GenAI-CDIO Authentic Assessment in Embedded Systems Design Course
PY  - 2025
Y1  - 2025
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Teaching, Assessment, and Learning for Engineering (TALE)
SP  - 1
EP  - 8
DO  - 10.1109/tale66047.2025.11346776
AB  - This study evaluates the impact of a Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI)-empowered Conceive-Design-Implement-Operate (CDIO) framework, integrated with Authentic Assessment (AA) and Challenge-Based Learning (CBL), in a 14-week Year 3 Embedded Systems Design course for 300 engineering undergraduates within a four-year engineering programme. The coursework design adopts AA's real-world relevance and CBL's open-ended challenges, focusing on the CDIO engineering design process to foster holistic embedded system design competencies. Grounded in constructivist and experiential learning theories, the framework leverages GenAI to support active knowledge construction, critical thinking, and practical application, aligning with Bloom's Taxonomy to develop higher-order skills. Students engaged in a 10-week group project to design a "two-wheeled self-balancing remote-controlled robot", structured in two cohesive phases, each employing a full GenAI-CDIO workflow, following 4 weeks of foundational training using "lean teaching approach". Quantitative analysis shows significant overall performance gains: A grades rose from 26.19% to 52.68%, failure rates dropped from 14.29% to 8.72%, and the closed-book examination component mean marks improved from 48.6 to 65 compared to the prior cohort. Survey responses from 119 students (5-point Likert scale, mean scores >4, p<0.0001, Cohen's d: 1.12-1.76) indicate strong positive perceptions of enhanced embedded system understanding, higher-order thinking, GenAI proficiency, and real-world simulation of professional practice. These findings validate the framework's efficacy in fostering industry-relevant competencies. We advocate its broader adoption to transform engineering pedagogy and prepare graduates for AI-augmented professional environments. © 2025 IEEE.
