AB  - With the rapid development of artificial intelligence (AI) technology and its increasing application in education, this research presents new opportunities and challenges for ideological and political education reform in universities. This study focuses on the reform and practice of ideological and political education in human resources management courses empowered by AI, aiming to explore how to effectively leverage AI to enhance the quality and effectiveness of ideological and political education. Using a combination of literature analysis, questionnaire surveys, and case studies, this study provides an in-depth analysis of the current status, existing problems, and development trends of AI applications in ideological and political education. Based on this analysis, a strategy for ideological and political education reform in human resources management courses based on AI is proposed, including the construction of an intelligent teaching platform, the development of personalized learning resources, and the optimization of the course evaluation system. A one-year practical study conducted in the human resources management major at a university validated the feasibility and effectiveness of the proposed strategy. Results indicate that AI-enabled ideological and political education reform can significantly enhance students' learning interest, ideological and political literacy, and professional competence. This study provides a theoretical basis and practical guidance for the in-depth integration of AI and ideological and political education, and holds valuable reference value for promoting ideological and political education reform in human resources management and other majors. © 2026 The Authors.
