TI  - Technical and Market Feasibility Assessment of an AI-Enabled Digital Learning Platform for Vocational Education in Indonesia
PY  - 2026
Y1  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Conference on AI Innovations and Industry, ICAIII 2026 - Conference Proceedings
DO  - 10.1109/icaiii69475.2026.11521446
AB  - This study presents a comprehensive prefeasibility assessment of DigiLearn, a digital learning innovation developed by Politeknik Negeri Batam to support large-scale adoption of AI-driven and industry-oriented education in Indonesia. The initiative aligns with national digital transformation priorities and aims to strengthen the vocational learning ecosystem through scalable, high-quality online content anchored to competency-based curricula. The methodological framework integrates mixed-method data collection, including documentation review, field observations, structured interviews, and user surveys, combined with technical feasibility, scalability, and market-readiness analysis. Results indicate that DigiLearn has achieved Technology Readiness Level (TRL) 6, demonstrating operational stability in relevant environments, while its Marketing Readiness Level (MRL) remains at Level 3, reflecting an early stage of market penetration and commercialization planning. Technical evaluation shows adequate production infrastructure - studios, multimedia equipment, cloud-based LMS, and digital asset workflows - supported by qualified human resources. Market analysis confirms rising demand for flexible, industry-aligned digital learning across students, professionals, and corporate training sectors. However, challenges persist in user validation, digital rights protection, and content security, particularly due to reliance on third-party platforms such as YouTube. The study concludes that DigiLearn is technically feasible and strategically positioned for national adoption, provided that pilot testing, structured quality assurance, DRM-based content protection, and strengthened go-to-market strategies are implemented. This work highlights DigiLearn's potential to become a scalable AI-ready digital learning infrastructure capable of enhancing Indonesia's vocational education and supporting future industry workforce development © 2026 IEEE.
