lications for engineering education, suggesting that integrating VR technologies could lead to more dynamic and enhanced engineering curriculums. While promising, the variability in critical thinking scores indicates that further refinement of VR content may be necessary to effectively target all aspects of computational thinking. Research in this study is supported by NSF Project #1915520: Enhancing Additive Manufacturing Education with Virtual Reality and Cybersecurity. © American Society for Engineering Education, 2025.
