TI  - Construction of an AI-Assisted Teaching System for Safety Technology Management under Industry-Education Integration
PY  - 2026
Y1  - 2026
T2  - 2026 5th International Symposium on Robotics, Artificial Intelligence and Information Engineering, RAIIE 2026
SP  - 340
EP  - 345
DO  - 10.1109/raiie70320.2026.11566908
AB  - The rapid advancement of artificial intelligence (AI) has created new opportunities for transforming vocational education in safety technology management. However, existing teaching systems face critical challenges including disconnection between curriculum content and industrial practice, insufficient personalized instruction, and a lack of intelligent support mechanisms. This paper proposes a novel AI-assisted teaching system framework under the paradigm of industry-education integration, centered on the 'AnXiaoYing' intelligent service platform. The proposed system architecture implements a four-stage progressive pedagogy: theoretical instruction, virtual simulation training, onsite operational practice, and competency assessment. To support large-scale, low-latency immersive training, we further introduce an edge-caching and asynchronous VR rendering pipeline, and to enable broader deployment we incorporate a multilingual NLP layer coupled with localized safety-regulation knowledge bases. A quasi-experimental study involving 156 students across two semesters demonstrates that the proposed system significantly improves students' safety risk identification accuracy by 23.7%, hazard control proficiency by 19.4%, and emergency decisionmaking competency by 28.1% compared to conventional teaching methods. A planned multi-institutional rollout across nine partner colleges and a 2 4-month longitudinal retention protocol are presented to validate generalizability and sustained competency maintenance. The results validate the effectiveness of deep AIindustry integration in cultivating compound safety management professionals. © 2026 IEEE.
