TI  - Data-Driven SEM and Clustering Analysis of Pre-service Teachers’ AI Literacy
PY  - 2026
Y1  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of 2025 2nd International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Future Education, AIFE 2025
SP  - 557
EP  - 561
DO  - 10.1145/3785987.3786081
AB  - AI literacy has become a core competency for pre-service teachers in the era of educational digitalization. This study integrates the UTAUT, SDT, and AI-TPACK frameworks to model the formation of AI literacy and employs structural equation modeling (SEM) for path validation, supplemented by K-means clustering for profiling literacy-level subgroups. Using questionnaire data (N = 186), SEM with 5,000 bootstrap resamples shows that AI-TPACK significantly predicts performance and effort expectancy, intrinsic motivation strongly predicts behavioral intention, and facilitating conditions also enhance behavioral intention (all p <.05). Clustering further reveals a high-literacy group characterized by higher AI-TPACK and intrinsic motivation, providing evidence for tiered training strategies. Although AIL was retained as the conceptual downstream outcome to highlight the role of facilitating conditions, the Lean-12 questionnaire measured only five proximal constructs (IM, AI-TPACK, PE, EE, BI) for parsimony.The results demonstrate a theory-data-technology synergy and offer computer-assisted evidence for improving AI literacy in teacher-education programs. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
