AB  - With the comprehensive promotion of 'curriculum ideology and politics,' integrating Ideological and Political Education (IPE) into foreign language courses has become a critical objective in Chinese higher education. However, achieving a natural and effective fusion remains a challenge. This study explores the application of Artificial Intelligence (AI) to empower this integration. We propose an Ideological and Political Sentiment Integration (IPSI) algorithm to quantitatively assess and select teaching materials that align with IPE objectives. A 15-week quasiexperimental study was conducted with two university classes (N=100) to evaluate the effectiveness of an AI-empowered teaching framework versus a traditional approach. The experimental group utilized an AI platform for personalized content recommendation, sentiment analysis of student discussions, and interactive case studies on Chinese culture. Pre- and post-intervention data on students' IPE awareness, cultural confidence, and critical thinking skills were collected through validated scales and analyzed using SPSS. Results from Independent Samples T-tests, Paired Samples T-tests, and ANCOVA revealed that the experimental group demonstrated statistically significant improvements in all measured dimensions (p<0.001) compared to the control group. These findings indicate that AI technology can serve as a powerful tool to enhance the depth and effectiveness of IPE in foreign language teaching, fostering students' national identity and crosscultural competence in a data-driven, personalized, and engaging manner. © 2025 IEEE.
N2  - With the comprehensive promotion of 'curriculum ideology and politics,' integrating Ideological and Political Education (IPE) into foreign language courses has become a critical objective in Chinese higher education. However, achieving a natural and effective fusion remains a challenge. This study explores the application of Artificial Intelligence (AI) to empower this integration. We propose an Ideological and Political Sentiment Integration (IPSI) algorithm to quantitatively assess and select teaching materials that align with IPE objectives. A 15-week quasiexperimental study was conducted with two university classes (N=100) to evaluate the effectiveness of an AI-empowered teaching framework versus a traditional approach. The experimental group utilized an AI platform for personalized content recommendation, sentiment analysis of student discussions, and interactive case studies on Chinese culture. Pre- and post-intervention data on students' IPE awareness, cultural confidence, and critical thinking skills were collected through validated scales and analyzed using SPSS. Results from Independent Samples T-tests, Paired Samples T-tests, and ANCOVA revealed that the experimental group demonstrated statistically significant improvements in all measured dimensions (p<0.001) compared to the control group. These findings indicate that AI technology can serve as a powerful tool to enhance the depth and effectiveness of IPE in foreign language teaching, fostering students' national identity and crosscultural competence in a data-driven, personalized, and engaging manner. © 2025 IEEE.
