TI  - Research on the Composition and Cultivation of Teacher Competence in Vocational Colleges Based Machine Learning and Deep Learning Methods
PY  - 2025
Y1  - 2025
T2  - International Conference on Communication, Computer and Information Technology, IC3IT 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ic3it66137.2025.11341150
AB  - In modern times, composition and cultivation of teacher competence in vocational colleges become an essential part to enhance quality of teaching and meet increasing demands of technology-driven education approaches. Here, competence of teacher involves pedagogical knowledge, professional skills, and capability to adapt to varying industrial and digital trends. To obtain more effective and constant evaluation phenomena, Machine Learning (ML) and Deep Learning (DL) methods have been gradually employed to identify large-scale educational data. These models allow predictive assessment, automated feedback generation and identification of important competence factors. However, existing systems still struggle with many limitations labeled data, less interpretability and adaptability and high computational cost. The motivation behind this study rises from requirement for intelligent systems which integrates reliability, interpretability and realistic adaptability for teacher evaluation and growth. This paper is about a comprehensive research of ML and DL-based techniques utilized to model teacher competence in vocational colleges. Further, identifies their performance, advantages and challenges across structured and unstructured data scenes. Additionally, study analyses existing research gaps and proposes requirement of hybrid and explainable Artificial Intelligence (AI)-based methods which efficiently bridge gap among theoretical improvements and practical implementation in real-world vocational education. © 2025 IEEE.
