AB  - This article presents an adaptive method for determining the variances of model errors in the structure of the Kalman filter, applied to dynamic systems with variable load. The method relies on the real-time discrepancy between predicted and measured values to update the variances in the system's dynamic model. The approach has been validated on an electrohydraulic system, where both the load condition and the angular velocity of the drive shaft are estimated using an extended Kalman filter structure. The results demonstrate improved estimation accuracy under conditions of unstable dynamics. The study also addresses metrological aspects related to the influence of model uncertainty on the final estimate, which is critical for enhancing the reliability of measurement applications.
