AB  - This paper analyzes the transformative influence of managed services on the telecommunications value chain amidst the arrival of 5G technology. Managed services have assumed multifaceted roles within contemporary telecom markets, reshaping the value chain significantly over the past decades. However, their significance in the 5G era surpasses that of preceding mobile generations, endowing network vendors with increased authority. The evolution is primarily attributed to the introduction of novel technologies and provisions inherent in 5G networks. Unlike previous generations, network operators find themselves unable to independently construct their 5G infrastructure, thereby shifting the strategic landscape in favour of vendors. This paradigm shift underscores the pivotal role of specialized vendors in optimizing 5G networks to address the unique challenges posed by this high-speed, low-latency technology. Managed services integration in 5G heralds a paradigmatic shift in telecom value chains, revolutionizing network design, deployment, and maintenance methodologies. In addition to traditional responsibilities, managed service providers now contribute to network security, proactive monitoring, and dynamic optimization, ensuring heightened reliability and efficiency. This transformative impact empowers vendors to navigate the complex telecom landscape and unlock the full potential of 5G technologies.
