T2  - 2021 3rd International Symposium on Material and Electrical Engineering Conference (ISMEE)
SP  - 166
EP  - 171
DO  - 10.1109/ismee54273.2021.9774081
AB  - DC motor is one type of actuator which is still widely used in control technology both in industry and in households. DC motors have a fast response but can be tricked by controlling the system to produce maximum response Control generally uses PID control. To design the desired response can be done by simulation using a mathematical model that has been validated to represent the DC motor system well. Therefore, students need to be supported by interactive learning media with DC motor validation systems to improve abilities and competencies. This final project aims to design a model validation system of brushed dc motor as an interactive learning media. This model validation system uses LabVIEW as interface software and NI ELVIS II as controller hardware and system data acquisition. This final project produces a mechanical construction with two identical motors whose parameters will identify. Parameters to be searched are armature coil resistance, Rm, armature coil inductance, La, motor torque constant, Km, moment inertia, J, and viscous damping friction, B. Rm and La were determined from the static test, Km, B, and J determined from the dynamic test. The minimum RMSE value of the model validity occurs at a voltage of 3-12V with an RMSE value below 10%. The results of the questionnaire show that the respondents gave a score of 80% regarding the quality of the overall system interface. In addition, the interface of the DC motor model validation system is considered feasible to be used as a teaching aid.
