AB  - Peer assessment has gained growing attention as a strategy to enhance collaborative learning, critical thinking, and student engagement. Despite its benefits, implementing peer assessment poses various logistical challenges. To address these issues, we designed and developed LearnEval, an innovative peer assessment platform that provides comprehensive support for diverse instructional contexts and workflows. This keynote paper reports on a seven-year deployment of LearnEval across several computer engineering courses. We provide an overview of the platform’s design principles and functionalities, and we describe the course settings in which peer assessment was applied. We also present a summary of the findings and share our long-term experience with the system. Results are encouraging, indicating that LearnEval usability is perceived as good, with the majority of students being satisfied and engaged with the platform.
