AB  - Learning pattern is a concept that integrates several dimensions (factors): motivation to learn, conception of learning, regulation strategies, and strategies for processing learning content according to Vermunt's model. There are four learning patterns that are formed by the combination of the four previous dimensions. The four learning patterns are: meaning-directed learning (M.D.) pattern, application-directed learning (A.D.) pattern, reproduction-directed learning (R.D.) pattern, and undirected learning (U.D.) pattern. This preliminary study seeks to identify learning patterns in first-year engineering students. To do so, Vermunt's Learning Styles Inventory (ILS) was applied to a sample of 120 first-year engineering students from a Chilean university. As results, the reliability analysis yielded satisfactory coefficients and the exploratory factor analysis confirmed the existence of four learning patterns, in accordance with Vermunt's research.
