gs suggests that 1) females engage in self-reflection more than males; 2) graduate student mentors in hybrid/wet labs are more insightful than those in dry labs; and 3) Non-engineering graduate student mentors are more insightful than engineering graduate student mentors. Ongoing research, including qualitative interviews to identify the self-reflective practices and influences of engineering graduate student researcher mentors, will uncover existing reflection strategies. Future research will also focus on developing a scale that measures self-awareness-related dimensions within STEMM mentoring relationships. © American Society for Engineering Education, 2024.
